# Vercel deploys this repo's ROOT -- api/ and public/. Everything listed here is
# either a different deploy target or a local artifact, and none of it is served.
#
# This file only matters for CLI deploys (`vercel --prod`), which upload the
# working directory rather than a git tree. Without it the deploy dies on
# "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)": pulse/pulse.db is a 600MB+ SQLite cache
# of raw heart-rate samples. Git-based deploys never hit this, because that file
# is gitignored and git only ever sends committed content -- which is exactly
# why it stayed invisible until the first CLI deploy.

# The Google Health sync. Runs on GitHub Actions, never on Vercel: its own
# README and .github/workflows/sync.yml own this half of the project.
pulse/

# Local tooling and generated artifacts.
.claude/
preview.html
